    <!--
      Generated. A restrained hue wheel, twenty four steps of fifteen degrees,
      for the custom colour a hex code is snapped to.

      The tones are solved per hue for a contrast ratio rather than fixed in
      HSL, because a fixed lightness is not perceptually even: yellow and blue
      at the same lightness are nowhere near the same darkness. Primary sits at
      5:1 against white, which every hue here clears, so the app bar carries its
      white text everywhere on the wheel; primaryDark at 8.5:1; the accent at
      the lightness where its contrast against a light and a dark background is
      equal, since it is used as text on both. Saturation is held well below the
      Material 500 level, which is the point of the set.

      Regenerate rather than hand-edit; the ratios above are the source of truth.
    -->
